  "foaf:name": "Mapping Atlantic Cold-Water Corals",
  "sdo:name": "Mapping Atlantic Cold-Water Corals",
  "sdo:description": "Cold-water corals (CWC) are vital to deep-sea ecosystems but face growing threats from human activities like fishing, mining, and climate change. To protect them, we need to understand where they thrive and how environmental changes impact their survival. While the North Atlantic has good data on CWC distribution, the Central and South Atlantic lack sufficient research. However, large amounts of previously inaccessible imagery data, including from oil and gas industries, are now available for analysis. This project unites experts to analyze these datasets, map CWC habitats, and develop artificial intelligence tools to improve efficiency. By creating high-resolution maps of current and future coral distribution, we will identify key areas for conservation. We will train new CWC scientists from lower- and middle-income countries, foster international collaboration and ensure that our scientific findings guide policies to protect these fragile ecosystems for the future.",
  "sdo:location": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Northern Ireland (UK)",
  "sdo:identifier": "16.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/mapping-atlantic-cold-water-corals/",
